 "direction_guard": 1.035276,
 "finding": "Telling one layout from another is bounded as detection is, and depth ambiguity does not rescue a reader: the same-depth bound holds for every allowed vertical transformation. Under Giza's regional microseism level the oracle, told everything but which layout is there, tells an L-shaped from a straight tunnel with detection minus false alarm at most 3.9e-07, and a column with a spiral from a plain column at most 5.3e-07; the tight bound gives 2.6e-09 and 9.1e-09 (each layout against empty ground, summed); the loose certificate with the background, the same way, caps discrimination at 5.110% at 5% for every pair. Discrimination needs 1.2 to 4.1 times the signal that detecting the first layout needs. With a lorry bouncing beside the layouts all pass, known exactly, at the worst of four sampled sides, the oracle's bound for the hardest-to-exclude pair (L_tunnel vs branching_tunnel) reaches 0.30 at 68 Hz: found <= false alarms + 0.30, so 95% / 5% is excluded (until the signal grows 4.2 times) though weaker, possibly useful performance is not. Only these layouts, this rock and these sources are covered."
}